<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/1st-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Beth Horon (66)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">66 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-jewish-roman-war">First Jewish–Roman War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Beth Horon was fought in the autumn of 66 CE, when Jewish rebels ambushed the retreating army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cestius-gallus">Cestius Gallus</a>, the Roman governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>, in the Beth Horon pass north-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>. According to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/josephus">Josephus</a> the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> lost nearly 6,000 men, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legio-xii-fulminata">Legio XII Fulminata</a> lost its eagle. The victory encouraged the revolt and led to the formation of a Jewish provisional government in Jerusalem.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-beth-horon-66.jpg" alt="Battle of Beth Horon (66)" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was מיכאלי at Hebrew Wikipedia. · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Beit_Horon.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
